    <div class="fl-scroll"><table id="fl-airlines"></table></div>

    <h2>Trends</h2>
    <p class="fl-note" style="margin:0 0 0.4rem">Every year from 2018 on. Your picked years are highlighted.</p>
    <div class="fl-charts">
      <div><h3>Flights a day</h3><div class="fl-bars" id="fl-tr-flights"></div><div class="fl-ticks" id="fl-tr-flights-t"></div><p class="fl-note" id="fl-tr-flights-n"></p></div>
      <div><h3>On time</h3><div class="fl-bars" id="fl-tr-ontime"></div><div class="fl-ticks" id="fl-tr-ontime-t"></div><p class="fl-note" id="fl-tr-ontime-n"></p></div>
    </div>
    <h3>Airline share of flights</h3>
    <div class="fl-scroll"><table id="fl-tr-mix"></table></div>

    <h2>When to fly</h2>
    <div class="fl-charts">
      <div><h3>On time by departure hour</h3><div class="fl-bars" id="fl-hour"></div><div class="fl-ticks" id="fl-hour-t"></div><p class="fl-note" id="fl-hour-n"></p></div>
      <div><h3>On time by day of week</h3><div class="fl-bars" id="fl-dow"></div><div class="fl-ticks" id="fl-dow-t"></div><p class="fl-note" id="fl-dow-n"></p></div>
      <div><h3>On time by month</h3><div class="fl-bars" id="fl-month"></div><div class="fl-ticks" id="fl-month-t"></div><p class="fl-note" id="fl-month-n"></p></div>
    </div>

    <h2>Why flights were late</h2>
    <p class="fl-note" style="margin:0 0 0.4rem">Share of all delay minutes, by cause</p>
    <div class="fl-causes" id="fl-causes"></div>
    <p class="fl-note" id="fl-cancels"></p>

    <h2>Fun facts</h2>
    <div class="fl-fun" id="fl-fun"></div>
  </div>
  </div>

  <section class="fl-how">
    <h2>How this page works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The data.</strong> Every domestic flight reported to the US Department of Transportation by the larger US airlines and their regional partners, January 2018 on, from the Bureau of Transportation Statistics. It doesn't include international flights or the smallest airlines.</li>
      <li><strong>On time.</strong> Each scheduled flight counts as exactly one of on time (arrived within 15 minutes of schedule), delayed, canceled, or diverted, so the four add up to 100%. That's the government's definition.</li>
      <li><strong>Airlines.</strong> Flights are listed under the airline you'd buy the ticket from, with the regional airline that flew it when they differ.</li>
      <li><strong>Updates.</strong> The data is refreshed monthly. The government publishes each month about two months later.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Sources</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Bureau of Transportation Statistics, <a href="https://www.transtats.bts.gov/DatabaseInfo.asp?QO_VQ=EFD&amp;DB_URL=" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Airline On-Time Performance Data</a> (Marketing Carrier On-Time Performance table)</li>
      <li><a href="https://registry.faa.gov/aircraftinquiry/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FAA Aircraft Registry</a>, for plane lookups</li>
      <li>Airline logos from <a href="https://www.travelpayouts.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Travelpayouts</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>
